Workflow: Prompt to Docs Generator

Purpose:
  Takes a simple human prompt and generates
  human-readable architecture docs in docs/.

Input:
  Simple text prompt
  Example:
    "Build an education platform for schools.
     Video conferencing, payments, AI search should be included.
     20K users in first 10 months, 1M in 2 years."

Output:
  docs/00-about/project.md
  docs/10-business/requirements.md
  docs/20-architecture/overview.md
  docs/30-backend/overview.md
  docs/40-frontend/overview.md
  docs/60-database/overview.md
  docs/70-api/overview.md
  docs/100-devops/overview.md
  docs/110-infrastructure/overview.md

Steps:
  1. PARSE_PROMPT:
      - Extract: purpose, users, features, constraints
      - Extract: scale (users, traffic)
      - Extract: mentioned technologies
      - Extract: non-functional requirements

  2. ANALYZE_REQUIREMENTS:
      - Map features to domains
      - Identify core vs nice-to-have
      - Identify technical challenges

  3. SELECT_TECH_STACK:
      - Choose backend language/framework
      - Choose frontend framework
      - Choose database
      - Choose infrastructure
      - Justify each choice in simple language

  4. DESIGN_ARCHITECTURE:
      - Choose architecture style (monolith/microservices)
      - Define domain boundaries
      - Define module structure

  5. GENERATE_DOCS:
      - Write each doc file in simple English
      - Include decision rationale
      - Include alternatives considered
      - Include risk assessment

  6. PRESENT_FOR_REVIEW:
      - Show docs to human
      - Collect feedback
      - Iterate until approved

Rules:
  [PG1] Docs MUST be in simple English, no jargon.
  [PG2] Every tech choice MUST have rationale.
  [PG3] Every architecture decision MUST have alternatives.
  [PG4] Scale requirements MUST drive infrastructure choices.
  [PG5] Security and compliance MUST be addressed.
  [PG6] Human MUST approve before .sdd/project/ generation.

State: +
